# Optional: LiteLLM and other app env (brain reads MCP URLs from mcp.json only).
# Copy to .env and adjust; docker-compose merges this with .env for the brain service.
#
# Stacks: run `mcp_servers/docker-compose.yaml` first (mongo, duckdb, *-mcp), then root `docker-compose.yaml` (brain).
# Both use Docker network `datacyber_mcp`. Catalog: mongo seeds `datacyber_catalog` via ../docker/mongo/init-catalog.js.
# UI catalog: GET /catalog/datasets on the brain calls MCP tool catalog_list_datasets (mcp.json → catalog server).
#
# CHAT_MODEL is required for /agent/chat (no default in code — must match LiteLLM GET /v1/models exactly).
# Example virtual-key routes (your proxy must expose these ids):
#   local/gemini-3-flash-preview
#   local/gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview
#   local/gemini-3.1-pro-preview
# Wrong id (common typo): local/gemini-3-pro-preview — not the same as local/gemini-3.1-pro-preview.
#
# DATACYBER_PIPELINE_DEBUG=1   # brain: include structured debug in POST /agent/chat JSON (see docs/PIPELINE_AND_DEBUG.md)
#
# Langfuse (optional): tracing for POST /agent/chat when both keys are set.
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-...
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-...
# LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://cloud.langfuse.com   # or https://us.cloud.langfuse.com / your self-hosted URL
# Self-hosted Langfuse on the SAME machine as Docker: do NOT use http://localhost:3000 — that is the container's
# loopback. Use http://host.docker.internal:3000 (brain compose maps host.docker.internal) or the host's LAN IP.
# Optional request headers: X-Langfuse-Session-Id, X-Langfuse-User-Id (sessions / users in Langfuse UI)
